# Q2. CPU Utilization Problem

### 1. Cause
- CPU utilization is only **30%** even though processes are ready.
- Processes keep moving between **Ready → Waiting → Ready**.
- This happens because they spend more time waiting for **I/O operations** than using the CPU.

### 2. Optimization
- Increase the number of processes (Multiprogramming).
- Use an efficient CPU scheduling algorithm.
- Reduce unnecessary I/O waiting.

### 3. Result
CPU utilization increases because the CPU can execute other ready processes while one process waits for I/O.
