# Q5. Context-Switch Overhead Debugging

### 1. Cause
- The scheduler uses a very small time quantum (**1 ms**).
- Threads are switched frequently before completing their execution.
- High I/O activity increases the number of context switches.

### 2. Optimizations
- Increase the time quantum.
- Reduce unnecessary context switching through better scheduling.

### 3. Result
The number of context switches decreases, CPU overhead is reduced, and system performance improves.
